{"ref":"BDB, תֹּ֫רֶן","hw":"תֹּ֫רֶן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">תֹּ֫רֶן</span></big>  <strong>n.m. mast (</strong>NH id.<em>;</em> √ unknown; Hoffm<sup>Ph. Inscr. 27 f.</sup> conj. <span dir=\"rtl\">תארן</span>, from <span dir=\"rtl\">ארן</span>, v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, אֹ֫רֶן\" href=\"/BDB,_אֹ֫רֶן\", dir=\"rtl\">אֹרֶן</a><strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳</span>, of Tyre as ship <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:5\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.5\">Ez 27:5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳ עַל־רֹאשׁ הָהָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 30:17\" href=\"/Isaiah.30.17\">Is 30:17</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">נֵס</span>), i.e. a (solitary) standard-pole, flag-staff; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">תָּרְנָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 33:23\" href=\"/Ezekiel.33.23\">33:23</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">נֵס</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲבָלִים</span>).","next":"BDB, תַּרְעֵלָה²","prev":"BDB, תָּרְמָה²"}